    IBM Watson color codes the confusion matrix to make it easier to read. Green indicates more
    correct and blue indicates less correct. What can you conclude?
    -> The green shading on the True Positive and True Negative cells tells you that your model is
        very good at predicting No Risk when the person is not a risk (True Positive) and Risk when
        the person is a risk (True Negative). 
    -> However, the AI model isn’t quite as good when it comes to False Positives (predicting
        someone is a Risk when they are not a risk) and False Negatives (predicting someone is No
        Risk when they are a risk). 

